This paper focuses on a system of quasilinear elliptic equations, specifically
\begin{equation*}
\begin{aligned}
\mathrm{div} \left( \frac{F_1(x,u)}{| \nabla u|^{p-1}} \nabla u_1 \right) &= 0, \\
\mathrm{div} \left( \frac{F_2(x,u)}{| \nabla u|^{p-1}} \nabla u_2 \right) &= 0,
\end{aligned}
\end{equation*}
in $R^N$, $N \geq 2$, where $p > 1$ and $F_1, F_2 \in C^1(R^{N-1} \times \mathbb{R}^2)$ are symmetric and non-constant. We prove that the system has a unique solution for any given boundary data in $C^1(\partial \Omega)$, where $\Omega$ is a bounded domain in $R^N$.
